)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@TUTORIAL: Acting on Jobs                       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  An action character in the NP column of a job acts on it. On the
}  Status panel:
}
{   H  }hold the job: a job waiting to execute does not start
{   A  }release it
{   C  }cancel it: it ends, its output stays
{   P  }purge it: it ends and its output is gone. SDSF does not ask
}        again, so be sure it is the right job.
{   O  }release its held output for printing
{   D  }JES2 displays the job's status in the log
}
}  SDSF gives the command to JES2 and says COMMAND ISSUED. JES2's answer
}  is in the log. Press Enter to see the job's new state.
}
}  You may act on your own jobs. The jobs of others need update access
}  in RAKF; without it: NOT AUTHORIZED FOR JOB.
}
}
}
}
}  Enter: next   PF10: back   PF7: list of parts   PF3: leave
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFTACT2
  &ZUP = ISFTUTOR
)END
